C o m p i l a t i o n


      Resevoir Operation Problem
       
      Taken from:
      HW3-LinearProgramingInGAMS.docx
      USU CEE 6410
      Dr. Rosenberg
       
      A reservoir is designed to provide water for irrigation. The reservoir has a capacity of 9,000 acre-
      feet. Initial storage is 3,000 acre-feet of water. The size of the diversion canal and farmed area is
      very large relative to the amount of irrigation water available, so there is no upper limit on usable
      irrigation water. Any water above the reservoir capacity must be released to the river (spill). The
      ending storage must be equal to or greater than the beginning storage. The benefits per unit of
      water, and the estimated inflows to the reservoir in 3 months are given in Table 1. What is the
      diversion schedule that maximizes benefits?
       
      Month   |   Inflow (acre-ft)   | Irrigation Benefits ($/acre-ft)
       
      June   |         5,000         |    150
      July   |         3,200         |    170
      August |         2,000         |    425
       
       
      Ammon Wallace
      CEE 6410
      ammon.wallace@usu.edu
  28   
  29  * 1. Define the Sets
  30  Sets
  31  t Time of Month /June, July, August/
  32  loc Location in the Network /Div, Res, Spill/;
  33   
  34   
  35  * 2. Define Input Data
  36  Parameters
  37      c(t) Objective Function Coeffiecients ($ per ac-ft)
  38      /June 150, July 170, August 425/
  39   
  40      inflow(t) Inflow input data (ac-ft)
  41      /June 5000, July 3200, August 2000/
  42   
  43      init_storage inital reservoir storage /3000/
  44      max_storage the max capacity of the reservoir/9000/;
  45   
  46  * 3. Define Variables
  47  Positive Variables
  48      X(loc, t) Decision Variables for location of water in the network for each month;
  49   
  50  Variables
  51      total_benefits the total amount of profit ($);
  52   
  53   
  54  * 4. Define equations
  55  Equations
  56      Profit Objective Function
  57      Capacity Reservoir Capacity
  58      Ending_Storage Ending storage must be greater than initial storage
  59      Mass_balance Mass balance equation;
  60   
  61  * Objective Function
  62  Profit.. total_benefits =E= sum(t, c(t)*X("Div", t));
  63   
  64   
  65  * Constrain Equations
  66  Capacity(t).. X("Res",t) =L= max_storage;
  67  Ending_Storage(t).. X("Res", "August") =G= init_storage;
  68  Mass_balance(t).. inflow(t) - X("Div",t) - X("Spill",t) =E= X("Res",t) - init_storage$(ord(t) eq 1)  - X("Res",t-1)$(ord(t) gt 1);
  69   
  70  * 5. Create the model using all of the defined equations
  71  Model Reservoir /all/;
  72   
  73   
  74  * 6. Solve the model and create a .lst file
  75  Solve Reservoir using LP maximing total_benefits;


